### Causal Diagram

In the field of causal inference, the I​C∗IC^{\ast} algorithm is a pivotal tool for identifying causal relationships among variables from observational data ([Pearl 2009](https://arxiv.org/html/2405.10746v2#bib.bib25)). This study employs the I​C∗IC^{\ast} algorithm to construct a causal graph, delineating the causal structures between variables XX,YY, and several covariates. The initial step of the I​C∗IC^{\ast} algorithm involves conducting conditional independence tests to analyze relationships among all pairs of variables within the dataset. This process relies on statistical tests to evaluate whether different combinations of variables are independent; if two variables are found to be dependent given other variables, an undirected edge is established between them.

